From: go-while <go-while@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:40:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Add end-to-end tests in Go

tests/e2e runs the real newscache binary against a fake upstream NNTP
server (github.com/go-while/nntp-testkit), in inetd mode (-i) and as a
standalone daemon (-n), with a generated config in a temp dir. Replies
are checked byte for byte (CRLF, dot-stuffing, stray bytes).

make check runs it through tests/e2e/run.sh when Go is installed and
reports it as skipped (exit 77) otherwise. By hand:

  cd tests/e2e && NEWSCACHE_BIN=../../src/newscache go test ./...

Each of the preceding fixes has a test in bugs_test.go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
